# `typeid` is comptime and takes a TYPE; a VALUE argument is an error. The
# message used to read "Use is() or downcast() ...", but there is no `is()` in
# the language — no BF_IS in src/expr.yo and no definition anywhere in src/ or
# std/ — so a user who followed the advice got a second, unrelated
# "Variable \"is\" not found". Pin the replacement, which names only APIs that
# exist (issues/fixed/typeid-diagnostic-suggests-a-nonexistent-is-builtin.md).
stdout_keep_match=downcast(value, T), which returns Option(T)
timeout=120
